{"diagnosis": "Loopback UART trap got 0x00 want 0xa5, so recv_buf_data latched 0x00 at stop state lines 89-94. recv_pattern never shifts because line 98 `recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:0]}` concatenates to 9 bits which truncates to unchanged pattern, leaving it stuck at reset 0. Correct right-shift for LSB-first (ser_tx = send_pattern[0] line 107) is `{ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]}`.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 			default: begin
 				if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
-					recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:0]};
+					recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 					recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 					recv_divcnt <= 0;
 				end
 			end
", "expected": "tohost PASS with uart loopback 0xa5 matched, no mismatch trap"}

